course: dictionary
lesson: 11113
title: Words for grown-ups
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: You may meet the word «whiskey» in a story, a film or a book. Use the context to work out its meaning. The sentence «whiskey is never for children» tells you that whiskey belongs to grown-ups, not to children.
explain: Whiskey is a strong alcoholic drink made from grain such as barley, corn or rye. Alcohol is harmful for young bodies, so whiskey is for adults only.
explain: The same drink can be spelled in different ways. Whiskey with an e is common in Ireland and the United States, and whisky without the e is common in Scotland. Both spellings are correct and both mean the same drink.
fact: Whiskey is a noun, and its plural is whiskeys.
fact: «Whiskey» means a strong alcoholic drink made from grain, for adults only.
fact: Grain such as barley, corn or rye is used to make whiskey.
fact: Children should never drink whiskey, because alcohol is harmful for young bodies.
fact: Whisky, without the e, is the spelling often used for the famous drink from Scotland.
exercise: «Whiskey is never for children.» Who is whiskey for? | Everyone at school | Children | *Adults only | Animals
exercise: What is whiskey made from? | Sand and water | Wood and paper | *Grain such as barley, corn or rye | Milk and sugar
exercise: Ella says whisky and whiskey are different drinks. What is true? | Whiskey is a fruit juice and whisky is a sweet | *They are two spellings of the same drink | Whiskey is for children and whisky is for adults | Whisky is a fizzy lemonade
test: What kind of drink is whiskey? | Fruit squash | Warm milk for bedtime | Fizzy lemonade | *A strong alcoholic drink for adults
test: Which country is famous for whisky? | *Scotland | Egypt | Japan | France
exam: Max says, «Hot whiskey will make my cold better.» What should you say? | *Whiskey is never for children, so tell an adult and ask for medicine | Whiskey is a fruit, so eat it | Ask for more whiskey | Good idea, have a big cup
